IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, s 27 (names of companies).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). s 27(2C), (2D), (3), (4) and (14) are shown "[Deleted by Act 36 of 2014]" and are not encoded (NOTES.md, coverage table).
-- Where the text says "in the Registrar's opinion" or "if the Registrar is satisfied", the opinion is a plain input (the Registrar's judgment is not guessed).
-- The statutes s 27 names (Business Names Registration Act 2014, Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005, Limited Partnerships Act 2008, VCC Act, Trade Marks Act 1998) are not sources: what they say is a fact the caller supplies.
-- Periods are counted by sg-periods.l4 only. "a period of at least N years has passed after the date" is read as: the day asked is after the last day of the N years (P1, P2; fork line F-I17).
-- Answers: JUST TRUE (the test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say). See the header of sgi-capacity.l4.

§ `Section 27(1): the names the Registrar must refuse`

-- (1): "Except with the Minister's consent or as provided in subsection (1B), the Registrar must refuse to register a company under this Act under a name which, in the Registrar's opinion —
-- (a) is undesirable; (b) is identical to the name of any other company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or corporation or to any registered business name; (c) is identical to a name reserved ...; or (d) is a name of a kind that the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept for registration."
-- The bar is the answer: JUST TRUE means the Registrar must refuse. Once the exception is met, or where no ground holds, the text does not say (NOTHING; fork line F-I18).
-- src:4667 | 27.—(1) Except with the Minister’s consent or as provided in
-- src:4668 | subsection (1B), the Registrar must refuse to register a company
-- src:4669 | under this Act under a name which, in the Registrar’s opinion —
-- src:4671 | (a) is undesirable;
-- src:4673 | (b) is identical to the name of any other company, limited
-- src:4674 | liability partnership, limited partnership or corporation or
-- src:4675 | to any registered business name;
-- src:4677 | (c) is identical to a name reserved under subsection (12B),
-- src:4678 | subsection (12B) as applied by section 357(2), or
-- src:4679 | section 378(15), section 16 of the Business Names
-- src:4680 | Registration Act 2014, section 23(4) of the Limited
-- src:4681 | Liability Partnerships Act 2005, section 17(4) of the
-- src:4682 | Limited Partnerships Act 2008, subsection (12B) as
-- src:4683 | applied by section 21(8) of the VCC Act, or
-- src:4684 | subsection (12B) as applied by section 133(2) of the
-- src:4685 | VCC Act; or
-- src:4687 | (d) is a name of a kind that the Minister has directed the
-- src:4688 | Registrar not to accept for registration.
@ref s 27(1) (src:4667-4688)
GIVEN `the Minister has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1B) applies to the name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Registrar's opinion the name is undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to the name of any other company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or corporation or to any registered business name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to a name reserved under subsection (12B) or under a provision paragraph (c) lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is a name of a kind that the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the company under the name` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has consented` OR `subsection (1B) applies to the name`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except with the Minister's consent or as provided in subsection (1B)" -- once the exception is met the text does not say what the Registrar does (fork line F-I18)
    ELSE (IF    `in the Registrar's opinion the name is undesirable`
             OR `in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to the name of any other company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or corporation or to any registered business name`
             OR `in the Registrar's opinion the name is identical to a name reserved under subsection (12B) or under a provision paragraph (c) lists`
             OR `the name is a name of a kind that the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept for registration`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must refuse to register a company ... under a name which, in the Registrar's opinion — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ..." -- a name outside the four paragraphs is not addressed by this subsection

§ `Section 27(1A): the names of dissolved or cancelled bodies, and how long they are kept`

-- The table of (1A)(a) to (f): each earlier holder of the name, and the years the Registrar keeps the name from registration ("a period of at least N years has passed after the date").
DECLARE `s 27(1A) earlier holder of the name` IS ONE OF
    `s 27(1A)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 27(1A)(a)(ii) a company dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A`
    `s 27(1A)(b) a person whose registration and registration of the business name has been cancelled under the Business Names Registration Act 2014 or had ceased under section 22 of that Act`
    `s 27(1A)(c) a foreign company notice of the dissolution of which has been given to the Registrar under section 377(2)`
    `s 27(1A)(d)(i) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its winding up under section 39 of, and the Fifth Schedule to, the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    `s 27(1A)(d)(ii) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 63 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    `s 27(1A)(e)(i) a limited partnership the registration of which was cancelled under section 14(1) or 19(4) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008`
    `s 27(1A)(e)(ii) a limited partnership of which notice was lodged with the Registrar of Limited Partnerships that it was dissolved under section 19(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008`
    `s 27(1A)(f)(i) a VCC dissolved following its winding up under Part 11 of the VCC Act`
    `s 27(1A)(f)(ii) a VCC dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A as applied by section 130B of the VCC Act`

