GIVEN holder IS A `s 27(1A) earlier holder of the name`
      `the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the dissolution, cancellation or cessation` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Minister has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1A) the Registrar must refuse to register the company under the name` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must, on or after 3 January 2016, ... refuse" (a date the text fixes in its own words; before it subsection (1A) does not bind)
    ELSE (IF (NOT `the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder`)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "refuse to register a company under a name, if — (a) it is identical to the name of a company that was dissolved ..." (a condition the text introduces with "if"; reading (a), fork line F-I4)
          ELSE (IF `the Minister has consented`
                THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except with the Minister's consent" -- once the exception is met the text does not say what the Registrar does (fork line F-I18)
                ELSE (IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the dissolution, cancellation or cessation` (`s 27(1A) the years that must pass after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` holder) Years
                      THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless ... a period of at least N years has passed" is met; the text then says nothing of whether the Registrar must or may register (fork line F-I18)
                      ELSE JUST TRUE)))

§ `Section 27(1B): names the Registrar may register despite subsection (1)`

-- (1B): "Despite subsection (1), the Registrar may, on or after 3 January 2016, register a company under (a) a name that is identical to the name of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11 —
-- (i) in respect of which notice was lodged under section 377(1) that the foreign company has ceased ..., if a period of at least 3 months has passed after the date of cessation; and (ii) the name of which was struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10), if a period of at least 6 years has passed after the date the name was so struck off; or
-- (b) a name that is identical to the name of a limited partnership in respect of which notice was lodged under section 19(1) ... that the limited partnership ceased to carry on business in Singapore, if a period of at least one year has passed after the date of cessation."
-- (a)(i) and (a)(ii) are joined by "and" in the text: both must be met for (a). That is the literal reading; the reading "or" is the other (fork line F-I16).
-- src:4778 | (1B) Despite subsection (1), the Registrar may, on or after
-- src:4779 | 3 January 2016, register a company under —
-- src:4781 | (a) a name that is identical to the name of a foreign company
-- src:4782 | registered under Division 2 of Part 11 —
-- src:4784 | (i) in respect of which notice was lodged under
-- src:4785 | section 377(1) that the foreign company has ceased
-- src:4786 | to have a place of business in Singapore or ceased to
-- src:4787 | carry on business in Singapore, if a period of at least
-- src:4788 | 3 months has passed after the date of cessation; and
-- src:4790 | (ii) the name of which was struck off the register under
-- src:4791 | section 377(8), (9) or (10), if a period of at least
-- src:4792 | 6 years has passed after the date the name was so
-- src:4793 | struck off; or
-- src:4795 | (b) a name that is identical to the name of a limited partnership
-- src:4796 | in respect of which notice was lodged under section 19(1)
-- src:4797 | of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that the limited
-- src:4802 | partnership ceased to carry on business in Singapore, if a
-- src:4803 | period of at least one year has passed after the date of
-- src:4804 | cessation.
@ref s 27(1B) (src:4778-4804)
GIVEN `the name is identical to the name of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was lodged under section 377(1) that the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore or ceased to carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the foreign company's cessation` IS A DATE
      `the name of the foreign company was struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the name of the foreign company was so struck off` IS A DATE
      `the name is identical to the name of a limited partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that the limited partnership ceased to carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the limited partnership's cessation` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1B) the Registrar may register the company under the name` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar may, on or after 3 January 2016, register" (a date the text fixes in its own words)
    ELSE (IF    (    `the name is identical to the name of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11`
                 AND `notice was lodged under section 377(1) that the foreign company has ceased to have a place of business in Singapore or ceased to carry on business in Singapore`
                 AND `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the foreign company's cessation` 3 Months
                 AND `the name of the foreign company was struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10)`
                 AND `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the name of the foreign company was so struck off` 6 Years)
             OR (    `the name is identical to the name of a limited partnership`
                 AND `notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that the limited partnership ceased to carry on business in Singapore`
                 AND `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the limited partnership's cessation` 1 Years)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Registrar may ... register a company under (a) ... if a period of at least 3 months has passed ...; and ... (b) ... if a period of at least one year has passed" -- a power whose "if" gates failed (fork lines F-I2 and F-I16)

§ `Section 27(2) and (2A): a direction to change a name, and who may ask for one`

-- (2): "Despite anything in this section and section 28 (other than section 28(4)), where the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered ... by a name — (a) which is one that is not permitted ...; (aa) ...; (ab) ...; (b) which so nearly resembles ...; or (c) the use of which has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- the Registrar may direct the firstmentioned company to change its name". A power gated by "where": split site (ii), NOTHING under the grant ruling (fork line F-I19).
-- src:4808 | (2) Despite anything in this section and section 28 (other than
-- src:4809 | section 28(4)), where the Registrar is satisfied that the company has
-- src:4810 | been registered (whether through inadvertence or otherwise and
-- src:4811 | whether before, on or after 30 January 2006) by a name —
-- src:4813 | (a) which is one that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:4814 | subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d);
-- src:4816 | (aa) which is one that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:4817 | subsection (1A) until the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:4818 | mentioned in that subsection;
-- src:4820 | (ab) which is one that is permitted to be registered under
-- src:4821 | subsection (1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:4822 | mentioned in that subsection;
-- src:4824 | (b) which so nearly resembles the name of any other company,
-- src:4825 | or any corporation, limited liability partnership, limited
-- src:4826 | partnership or registered business name, as to be likely to
-- src:4827 | be mistaken for it; or
-- src:4829 | (c) the use of which has been restrained by an injunction
-- src:4830 | granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- src:4832 | the Registrar may direct the firstmentioned company to change its
-- src:4833 | name, and the company must comply with the direction within
-- src:4834 | 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the
-- src:4835 | Registrar may allow, unless the direction is annulled by the Minister.
@ref s 27(2) (src:4808-4835)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1A) until the expiry of the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is permitted to be registered under subsection (1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that so nearly resembles the name of any other company, or any corporation, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or registered business name, as to be likely to be mistaken for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name the use of which has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) the Registrar may direct the company to change its name` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d)`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1A) until the expiry of the relevant period`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that is permitted to be registered under subsection (1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name that so nearly resembles the name of any other company, or any corporation, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or registered business name, as to be likely to be mistaken for it`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered by a name the use of which has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the Registrar is satisfied that the company has been registered ... by a name — (a) ...; (aa) ...; (ab) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..., the Registrar may direct" -- a power gated by "where"; split site (ii), fork line F-I19

-- (2), second limb: "and the company must comply with the direction within 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow, unless the direction is annulled by the Minister."
-- The deadline is the later of 6 weeks and the longer period allowed. "unless ... annulled" once met: the text is silent (NOTHING; fork line F-I18).
