-- src:4820 | (ab) which is one that is permitted to be registered under
-- src:4821 | subsection (1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:4822 | mentioned in that subsection;
-- src:4824 | (b) which so nearly resembles the name of any other company,
-- src:4825 | or any corporation, limited liability partnership, limited
-- src:4826 | partnership or registered business name, as to be likely to
-- src:4827 | be mistaken for it; or
-- src:4829 | (c) the use of which has been restrained by an injunction
-- src:4830 | granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- src:4832 | the Registrar may direct the firstmentioned company to change its
-- src:4833 | name, and the company must comply with the direction within
-- src:4834 | 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the
-- src:4835 | Registrar may allow, unless the direction is annulled by the Minister.
@ref s 27(2) (src:4808-4835)
GIVEN `the day of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A DATE
      `the Minister has annulled the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has changed its name as directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company changed its name` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) the company has complied with the direction` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has annulled the direction`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the direction is annulled by the Minister" -- once met, the duty to comply is gone and the text says nothing of the company's position (fork line F-I18)
    ELSE (IF `the company has changed its name as directed`
          THEN (IF `the day the company changed its name` AT MOST `s 27(2) the last day for compliance` `the day of the direction` `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must comply with the direction within 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)
          ELSE (IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `s 27(2) the last day for compliance` `the day of the direction` `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the period has run and the name is not changed
                ELSE NOTHING))    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period has not run, and the text does not say the duty is met or unmet before then

GIVEN `the day of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 27(2) the last day for compliance` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` AND (`the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the direction` 6 Weeks)
    THEN `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed`
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the direction` 6 Weeks

DECLARE `s 27(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 27(2) change the company's name as the Registrar has directed`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. Time 0 is the date of the direction; the days allowed are 42 (6 weeks) or the longer period the Registrar allows.
-- src:4808 | (2) Despite anything in this section and section 28 (other than
-- src:4809 | section 28(4)), where the Registrar is satisfied that the company has
-- src:4810 | been registered (whether through inadvertence or otherwise and
-- src:4811 | whether before, on or after 30 January 2006) by a name —
-- src:4813 | (a) which is one that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:4814 | subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d);
-- src:4816 | (aa) which is one that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:4817 | subsection (1A) until the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:4818 | mentioned in that subsection;
-- src:4820 | (ab) which is one that is permitted to be registered under
-- src:4821 | subsection (1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:4822 | mentioned in that subsection;
-- src:4824 | (b) which so nearly resembles the name of any other company,
-- src:4825 | or any corporation, limited liability partnership, limited
-- src:4826 | partnership or registered business name, as to be likely to
-- src:4827 | be mistaken for it; or
-- src:4829 | (c) the use of which has been restrained by an injunction
-- src:4830 | granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- src:4832 | the Registrar may direct the firstmentioned company to change its
-- src:4833 | name, and the company must comply with the direction within
-- src:4834 | 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the
-- src:4835 | Registrar may allow, unless the direction is annulled by the Minister.
@ref s 27(2) (src:4808-4835)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the company has to comply, being 42 or the longer period the Registrar allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 27(2) act`
`s 27(2) the company must change its name within 6 weeks of the direction` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 27(2) change the company's name as the Registrar has directed`
    WITHIN `the number of days the company has to comply, being 42 or the longer period the Registrar allows`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not change its name within 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the Registrar allowed"

-- (2A), first limb: "Any person may apply, in writing, to the Registrar to give a direction to a company under subsection (2) on a ground referred to in that subsection".
-- src:4839 | (2A) Any person may apply, in writing, to the Registrar to give a
-- src:4840 | direction to a company under subsection (2) on a ground referred to in
-- src:4841 | that subsection; but the Registrar must not consider any application to
-- src:4842 | give a direction to a company on the ground referred to in
-- src:4843 | subsection (2)(b) unless the Registrar receives the application
-- src:4844 | within 12 months from the date of incorporation of the company.
@ref s 27(2A) (src:4839-4844)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is on a ground referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2A) the person may apply to the Registrar for a direction to the company` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in writing` AND `the application is on a ground referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person may apply, in writing, ... on a ground referred to in that subsection" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- (2A), second limb: "the Registrar must not consider any application ... on the ground referred to in subsection (2)(b) unless the Registrar receives the application within 12 months from the date of incorporation of the company."
-- A bar: JUST TRUE means the Registrar must not consider the application. Within the 12 months the bar is lifted and the text is silent (NOTHING).
-- src:4839 | (2A) Any person may apply, in writing, to the Registrar to give a
-- src:4840 | direction to a company under subsection (2) on a ground referred to in
-- src:4841 | that subsection; but the Registrar must not consider any application to
-- src:4842 | give a direction to a company on the ground referred to in
-- src:4843 | subsection (2)(b) unless the Registrar receives the application
-- src:4844 | within 12 months from the date of incorporation of the company.
@ref s 27(2A) (src:4839-4844)
GIVEN `the application is on the ground referred to in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the company's incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the day the Registrar received the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2A) the Registrar is barred from considering the application` MEANS
    IF    `the application is on the ground referred to in subsection (2)(b)`
      AND `the day the Registrar received the application` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the company's incorporation` 12 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not consider any application ... on the ground referred to in subsection (2)(b) unless the Registrar receives the application within 12 months" -- the bar reaches that ground only; within the 12 months the text is silent

-- (2B): "If the company fails to comply with subsection (2), the company and its officers shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty."
-- src:4846 | (2B) If the company fails to comply with subsection (2), the
-- src:4847 | company and its officers shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:4852 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a
-- src:4853 | default penalty.
@ref s 27(2B) (src:4846-4853)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2B) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with subsection (2)` AND `the person is the company or an officer of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company fails to comply with subsection (2), the company and its officers shall be guilty of an offence" (the provision's own question; split site (i), fork line F-I10)

-- src:4846 | (2B) If the company fails to comply with subsection (2), the
-- src:4847 | company and its officers shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:4852 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a
-- src:4853 | default penalty.
@ref s 27(2B) (src:4846-4853)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 27(2B) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 27(2B) the person is guilty of the offence` `the company fails to comply with subsection (2)` `the person is the company or an officer of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $2,000 "and also to a default penalty"; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for a person it makes guilty

§ `Section 27(5) to (6): appeals to the Minister`

DECLARE `s 27(5) decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 27(5)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (2)`
    `s 27(5)(b) the Registrar's refusal to give a direction to a company under subsection (2) pursuant to an application under subsection (2A)`
    `s 27(5) another decision`

-- (5): "An appeal to the Minister against the following decisions of the Registrar that are made on or after 3 January 2016 may be made by the following persons within the following times: (a) ... by the company aggrieved by the decision within 30 days after the decision; and (b) ... by the applicant aggrieved by the refusal within 30 days after being informed of the refusal."
-- The persons and times are the text's own: the right person outside 30 days: JUST FALSE (the period ruling, item (a)); another person or decision: NOTHING (a list not closed with "only"); a decision made before 3 January 2016: NOTHING (the subsection does not reach it).
-- src:4863 | (5) An appeal to the Minister against the following decisions of the
-- src:4864 | Registrar that are made on or after 3 January 2016 may be made by
-- src:4865 | the following persons within the following times:
-- src:4867 | (a) in the case of the Registrar’s decision under
-- src:4868 | subsection (2) — by the company aggrieved by the
-- src:4869 | decision within 30 days after the decision; and
-- src:4871 | (b) in the case of the Registrar’s refusal to give a direction to a
-- src:4872 | company under subsection (2) pursuant to an application
-- src:4873 | under subsection (2A) — by the applicant aggrieved by the
-- src:4874 | refusal within 30 days after being informed of the refusal.
@ref s 27(5) (src:4863-4874)
GIVEN decision IS A `s 27(5) decision`
      `the person is the company aggrieved by the decision, or the applicant aggrieved by the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Registrar made the decision` IS A DATE
      `the day the applicant was informed of the refusal` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(5) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` MEANS
    IF decision EQUALS `s 27(5) another decision`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) lists two decisions and says nothing of any other
    ELSE (IF `the day the Registrar made the decision` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "decisions of the Registrar that are made on or after 3 January 2016" -- an earlier decision is outside the subsection
          ELSE (IF `the person is the company aggrieved by the decision, or the applicant aggrieved by the refusal`
                THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (IF decision EQUALS `s 27(5)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (2)` THEN `the day the Registrar made the decision` ELSE `the day the applicant was informed of the refusal`) `the day the appeal is made` 30 Days
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after the decision" / "within 30 days after being informed of the refusal" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the company aggrieved by the decision" / "by the applicant aggrieved by the refusal" -- the text names no other person

-- src:4878 | (5AA) The decision of the Minister on an appeal made under
-- src:4879 | subsection (5) is final.
@ref s 27(5AA) (src:4878-4879)
GIVEN `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal made under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(5AA) the decision of the Minister on the appeal is final` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal made under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The decision of the Minister on an appeal made under subsection (5) is final." says nothing of any other decision

-- src:4883 | (5A) To avoid doubt, where the Registrar makes a decision under
-- src:4884 | subsection (2) or the Minister makes a decision under subsection (5),
-- src:4885 | he or she must accept as correct any decision of the Court to grant an
-- src:4886 | injunction referred to in subsection (2)(c).
@ref s 27(5A) (src:4883-4886)
GIVEN `the decision is the Registrar's decision under subsection (2) or the Minister's decision under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has granted an injunction referred to in subsection (2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(5A) the Registrar or the Minister must accept as correct the decision of the Court to grant the injunction` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the Registrar's decision under subsection (2) or the Minister's decision under subsection (5)` AND `the Court has granted an injunction referred to in subsection (2)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the Registrar makes a decision under subsection (2) or the Minister makes a decision under subsection (5), he or she must accept as correct any decision of the Court to grant an injunction referred to in subsection (2)(c)" -- outside those decisions the subsection says nothing

-- src:4888 | (6) The Minister must cause a direction given by him or her under
-- src:4889 | subsection (1) to be published in the Gazette.
@ref s 27(6) (src:4888-4889)
GIVEN `the Minister has given a direction under subsection (1)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(6) the Minister must cause the direction to be published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has given a direction under subsection (1)(d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a direction given by him or her under subsection (1)" -- a direction not given under subsection (1) is outside it

§ `Section 27(7) to (9): the words in a name`

-- (7): "Subject to section 29, a limited company must have either 'Limited' or 'Berhad' as part of and at the end of its name." A limited company is s 4(1) "limited company" (sg-definitions.l4).
-- src:4891 | (7) Subject to section 29, a limited company must have either
-- src:4892 | “Limited” or “Berhad” as part of and at the end of its name.
@ref s 27(7) (src:4891-4892)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 29 exempts the company from the use of the word Limited or Berhad` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name has the word Limited or Berhad as part of the name and at the end of the name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(7) the name of the limited company has the word Limited or Berhad as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "limited company" the company is a limited company` liability `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `section 29 exempts the company from the use of the word Limited or Berhad`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 29" -- once an exemption applies the subsection says nothing
          ELSE (IF `the name has the word Limited or Berhad as part of the name and at the end of the name`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a limited company must have either 'Limited' or 'Berhad' as part of and at the end of its name"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a limited company"

-- (8): "A private company must have the word 'Private' or 'Sendirian' as part of its name, inserted immediately before the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' or, in the case of an unlimited company, at the end of its name."
-- src:4894 | (8) A private company must have the word “Private” or “Sendirian”
-- src:4895 | as part of its name, inserted immediately before the word “Limited”
-- src:4896 | or “Berhad” or, in the case of an unlimited company, at the end of its
-- src:4897 | name.
@ref s 27(8) (src:4894-4897)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the name has the word Private or Sendirian inserted immediately before the word Limited or Berhad` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name has the word Private or Sendirian at the end of the name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(8) the name of the private company has the word Private or Sendirian as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company`
    THEN (IF `s 4(1) "unlimited company" the company is an unlimited company` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN (IF `the name has the word Private or Sendirian at the end of the name`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of an unlimited company, at the end of its name"
          ELSE (IF `the name has the word Private or Sendirian inserted immediately before the word Limited or Berhad`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A private company must have the word 'Private' or 'Sendirian' as part of its name, inserted immediately before the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad'"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a private company"

DECLARE `s 27(9) use in a name` IS ONE OF
    `s 27(9)(a) the abbreviation Pte. in lieu of the word Private`
    `s 27(9)(a) the abbreviation Sdn. in lieu of the word Sendirian`
    `s 27(9)(b) the abbreviation Ltd. in lieu of the word Limited`
    `s 27(9)(b) the abbreviation Bhd. in lieu of the word Berhad`
    `s 27(9)(c) the word in lieu of its corresponding abbreviation`
    `s 27(9) another use`

-- (9): "It is lawful to use and no description of a company is deemed inadequate or incorrect by reason of the use of (a) ... (b) ... (c) ...".
-- src:4902 | (9) It is lawful to use and no description of a company is deemed
-- src:4903 | inadequate or incorrect by reason of the use of —
-- src:4905 | (a) the abbreviation “Pte.” in lieu of the word “Private” or the
-- src:4906 | abbreviation “Sdn.” in lieu of the word “Sendirian”
-- src:4907 | contained in the name of a company;
-- src:4909 | (b) the abbreviation “Ltd.” in lieu of the word “Limited” or the
-- src:4910 | abbreviation “Bhd.” in lieu of the word “Berhad”
-- src:4911 | contained in the name of a company; or
-- src:4913 | (c) any of such words in lieu of the corresponding abbreviation
-- src:4914 | contained in the name of a company.
@ref s 27(9) (src:4902-4914)
GIVEN use IS A `s 27(9) use in a name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(9) the use is lawful and does not make the description of the company inadequate or incorrect` MEANS
    CONSIDER use
    WHEN `s 27(9) another use` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (9) names three uses and does not say they are the only lawful ones
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 27(10) to (16): reserving a name`

-- src:4916 | (10) A person may apply in the prescribed form to the Registrar for
-- src:4917 | the reservation of a name set out in the application as —
-- src:4919 | (a) the name of an intended company; or
-- src:4921 | (b) the name to which a company proposes to change its name.
@ref s 27(10) (src:4916-4921)
GIVEN `the application is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is set out in the application as the name of an intended company, or as the name to which a company proposes to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(10) the person may apply to the Registrar for the reservation of the name` MEANS
    IF `the application is in the prescribed form` AND `the name is set out in the application as the name of an intended company, or as the name to which a company proposes to change its name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may apply in the prescribed form ... for the reservation of a name set out in the application as (a) ...; or (b) ..." -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- (11): "A company must not be registered under section 19(3) and the Registrar must not approve the change of name of a company under section 28(2) unless the name ... has been reserved under subsection (12)."
-- A bar: JUST TRUE means the registration or the approval is barred (the name has not been reserved). Once reserved the text is silent (NOTHING; fork line F-I18).
-- src:4925 | (11) A company must not be registered under section 19(3) and the
-- src:4926 | Registrar must not approve the change of name of a company under
-- src:4927 | section 28(2) unless the name which it is proposed to be registered or
-- src:4928 | the proposed new name (as the case may be) has been reserved under
-- src:4929 | subsection (12).
@ref s 27(11) (src:4925-4929)
GIVEN `the name has been reserved under subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(11) the registration of the company, or the approval of the change of name, is barred` MEANS
    IF `the name has been reserved under subsection (12)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless the name ... has been reserved under subsection (12)" is met; the text then says nothing of whether registration or approval follows (fork line F-I18)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (12): "The Registrar may approve an application made under subsection (10) only if the Registrar is satisfied that (a) the application is made in good faith; and (b) the name to be reserved is one in respect of which a company may be registered having regard to subsections (1), (1A) and (1B)."
-- src:4931 | (12) The Registrar may approve an application made under
-- src:4932 | subsection (10) only if the Registrar is satisfied that —
-- src:4934 | (a) the application is made in good faith; and
-- src:4936 | (b) the name to be reserved is one in respect of which a
-- src:4937 | company may be registered having regard to
-- src:4938 | subsections (1), (1A) and (1B).
@ref s 27(12) (src:4931-4938)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the application is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the name to be reserved is one in respect of which a company may be registered having regard to subsections (1), (1A) and (1B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(12) the Registrar may approve the application` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is satisfied that the application is made in good faith`
      AND `the Registrar is satisfied that the name to be reserved is one in respect of which a company may be registered having regard to subsections (1), (1A) and (1B)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may approve an application made under subsection (10) only if the Registrar is satisfied that (a) ...; and (b) ..." (a gate closed with "only if")

-- (12A): "The Registrar must refuse to approve an application to reserve a name under subsection (10) as the name of an intended company if the Registrar is satisfied that (a) ...; or (b) ...".
-- src:4942 | (12A) The Registrar must refuse to approve an application to
-- src:4943 | reserve a name under subsection (10) as the name of an intended
-- src:4944 | company if the Registrar is satisfied that —
-- src:4946 | (a) the name is for a company that is likely to be used for an
-- src:4947 | unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public
-- src:4948 | peace, welfare or good order in Singapore; or
-- src:4953 | (b) it would be contrary to the national security or interest for
-- src:4954 | the company to be registered.
@ref s 27(12A) (src:4942-4954)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the name is for a company that is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the company to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(12A) the Registrar must refuse to approve the application` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is satisfied that the name is for a company that is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the company to be registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must refuse to approve ... if the Registrar is satisfied that (a) ...; or (b) ..." (a condition the text introduces with "if"; a duty, so JUST FALSE; reading (a), fork line F-I4)

-- (12B): the reservation runs "for a period starting at the time the Registrar receives the application and ending (a) if the Registrar approves the application — 60 days after the date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant
-- that the application has been approved, or such further period of 60 days as the Registrar may, on application made in good faith, extend; or (b) if the Registrar refuses to approve the application — on the date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant of the refusal."
-- The number of further periods of 60 days is a plain input (the text says "such further period of 60 days", and s 27(13) the same: whether more than one extension is allowed is fork line F-I20).
-- src:4958 | (12B) Where an application for a reservation of a name is made
-- src:4959 | under subsection (10), the Registrar must reserve the proposed name
-- src:4960 | for a period starting at the time the Registrar receives the application
-- src:4961 | and ending —
-- src:4963 | (a) if the Registrar approves the application — 60 days after
-- src:4964 | the date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant that
-- src:4965 | the application has been approved, or such further period
-- src:4966 | of 60 days as the Registrar may, on application made in
-- src:4967 | good faith, extend; or
-- src:4969 | (b) if the Registrar refuses to approve the application — on the
-- src:4970 | date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant of the
-- src:4971 | refusal.
@ref s 27(12B) (src:4958-4971)
GIVEN `the Registrar approves the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Registrar notifies the applicant of the approval or the refusal` IS A DATE
      `the number of further periods of 60 days the Registrar has extended the reservation by` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 27(12B) the last day of the reservation` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar approves the application`
    THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the Registrar notifies the applicant of the approval or the refusal` (60 TIMES (1 PLUS `the number of further periods of 60 days the Registrar has extended the reservation by`)) Days
    ELSE `the day the Registrar notifies the applicant of the approval or the refusal`

-- src:4958 | (12B) Where an application for a reservation of a name is made
-- src:4959 | under subsection (10), the Registrar must reserve the proposed name
-- src:4960 | for a period starting at the time the Registrar receives the application
-- src:4961 | and ending —
-- src:4963 | (a) if the Registrar approves the application — 60 days after
-- src:4964 | the date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant that
-- src:4965 | the application has been approved, or such further period
-- src:4966 | of 60 days as the Registrar may, on application made in
-- src:4967 | good faith, extend; or
-- src:4969 | (b) if the Registrar refuses to approve the application — on the
-- src:4970 | date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant of the
-- src:4971 | refusal.
@ref s 27(12B) (src:4958-4971)
GIVEN `the application for reservation was made under subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Registrar received the application` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has notified the applicant of the approval or the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar approves the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Registrar notifies the applicant of the approval or the refusal` IS A DATE
      `the number of further periods of 60 days the Registrar has extended the reservation by` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(12B) the name is reserved on the day` MEANS
    IF `the application for reservation was made under subsection (10)`
    THEN (IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day the Registrar received the application`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period starting at the time the Registrar receives the application"
          ELSE (IF `the Registrar has notified the applicant of the approval or the refusal`
                THEN (IF `the date asked` AT MOST `s 27(12B) the last day of the reservation` `the Registrar approves the application` `the day the Registrar notifies the applicant of the approval or the refusal` `the number of further periods of 60 days the Registrar has extended the reservation by`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ending (a) ... 60 days after the date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant that the application has been approved ...; or (b) ... on the date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant of the refusal"
                ELSE JUST TRUE))   -- the reservation has started and no end has yet been fixed by a notification
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an application for a reservation of a name is made under subsection (10)" -- no such application, no reservation under this subsection

-- (12C): "A person aggrieved by a decision of the Registrar (a) refusing to approve an application under subsection (10); or (b) refusing an application under subsection (12B)(a) to extend the reservation period, may, within 30 days after being informed of the Registrar's decision, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final."
-- src:4975 | (12C) A person aggrieved by a decision of the Registrar —
-- src:4977 | (a) refusing to approve an application under subsection (10);
-- src:4978 | or
-- src:4980 | (b) refusing an application under subsection (12B)(a) to
-- src:4981 | extend the reservation period,
-- src:4983 | may, within 30 days after being informed of the Registrar’s decision,
-- src:4984 | appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 27(12C) (src:4975-4984)
GIVEN `the decision refuses to approve an application under subsection (10), or refuses an application under subsection (12B)(a) to extend the reservation period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person was informed of the Registrar's decision` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(12C) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision refuses to approve an application under subsection (10), or refuses an application under subsection (12B)(a) to extend the reservation period` AND `the person is aggrieved by the decision`
    THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the person was informed of the Registrar's decision` `the day the appeal is made` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 30 days after being informed of the Registrar's decision, appeal to the Minister" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person aggrieved by a decision of the Registrar (a) refusing ...; or (b) refusing ..." -- another person or decision is outside the subsection

-- (13): "If, at any time during a period for which a name is reserved, application is made to the Registrar for an extension of that period and the Registrar is satisfied as to the bona fides of the application, the Registrar may extend that period for a further period of 60 days."
-- src:4988 | (13) If, at any time during a period for which a name is reserved,
-- src:4989 | application is made to the Registrar for an extension of that period
-- src:4990 | and the Registrar is satisfied as to the bona fides of the application,
-- src:4991 | the Registrar may extend that period for a further period of 60 days.
@ref s 27(13) (src:4988-4991)
GIVEN `the application for an extension is made during a period for which the name is reserved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied as to the bona fides of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(13) the Registrar may extend the period for a further period of 60 days` MEANS
    IF `the application for an extension is made during a period for which the name is reserved` AND `the Registrar is satisfied as to the bona fides of the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, at any time during a period for which a name is reserved, application is made ... and the Registrar is satisfied as to the bona fides ..., the Registrar may extend" -- a power whose "If" gate failed; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-I2)

-- (15): "The reservation of a name under this section in respect of an intended company or company does not in itself entitle the intended company or company to be registered by that name, either originally or upon change of name."
-- src:4997 | (15) The reservation of a name under this section in respect of an
-- src:4998 | intended company or company does not in itself entitle the intended
-- src:4999 | company or company to be registered by that name, either originally
-- src:5000 | or upon change of name.
@ref s 27(15) (src:4997-5000)
GIVEN `the name is reserved under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(15) the reservation in itself entitles the company to be registered by the name` MEANS
    IF `the name is reserved under this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reservation of a name under this section ... does not in itself entitle the intended company or company to be registered by that name"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "the reservation of a name under this section"

-- (16): "In this section and section 28, 'registered business name' has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Business Names Registration Act 2014." The Act is not a source: whether the name is one is a supplied fact.
-- src:5007 | (16) In this section and section 28, “registered business name” has
-- src:5008 | the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Business Names
-- src:5009 | Registration Act 2014.
@ref s 27(16) (src:5007-5009)
GIVEN `the name is a registered business name as section 2(1) of the Business Names Registration Act 2014 gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(16) "registered business name" the name is a registered business name` MEANS
    IF `the name is a registered business name as section 2(1) of the Business Names Registration Act 2014 gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'registered business name' has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Business Names Registration Act 2014" (a definition that hands the meaning to another Act: closed, as the keel treats "limited liability partnership")
